WEBVTT

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:47.610
Hey, I'm hungry, Mikochi.

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:49.980
Jeez...

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:54.030
You could lend a hand carrying this thing, Hakumei.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:56.820
Can't. Not when I'm starving like this.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.490
You don't carry your weight at home, either...

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.790
Let's hurry up and eat!

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:04.910
Okay, already.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:29.610
We shouldn't have bought such a big dresser.

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:32.900
It might not even fit through the front door.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.530
I'm not sure what we should do.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:40.240
We could disassemble—

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:41.370
No, no.

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:48.960
Hakumei, your mug...

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:53.250
Are you okay?

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:55.470
I'm sorry.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:04.140
That was meant for guests, anyway.
We'll have to buy you a mug of your own.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.230
Great.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.480
Oh, the news-hopper!

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:15.610
Thanks for your business!

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.820
Mikochi! This is big news!

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.080
Someone saw an evening kite?

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:30.830
Yeah, a huge bird with deep red feathers!

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:32.460
Haven't you heard of it?

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:34.090
Of course I have.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:39.680
The fables say that it will grant one wish if you encounter it at dawn, right?

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:43.850
Someone apparently saw one fly off from the rocky hills at the north yesterday!

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:45.850
Sounds fishy to me.

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:49.140
I'm gonna go and capture that thing!

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:49.980
Huh?!

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:53.980
If we can tame it, it'll be a huge help for carrying luggage and going on trips.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:56.480
I'm ready to climb the mountain!

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.950
Wait a minute! I just got lunch ready.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:03.120
We can bring it with us and eat in the mountains.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:07.330
W-Wait! If we go now, it'll take us until morning to reach the top.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.620
And what will we do about the dresser?!

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:17.000
S-Slow down a bit...

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.510
Mikochi, you don't have that much stamina, huh?

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:24.850
It's more like... you have way too much of it...

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:37.780
<i>She's making a path for us.</i>

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:40.820
<i>Come to think of it, she did the same before...</i>

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.870
C'mon, you can do it!

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:54.250
I finally caught up.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:55.500
Good job.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.680
Want to have lunch soon?

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.300
Yeah, one sec.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.810
Let's ride on these guys' backs to get there.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:14.270
We can keep going while we eat.
That's killing two birds with one stone.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.810
Sure thing.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:32.120
Now this is the way to travel! Right, Mikochi?

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.920
I want to keep this guy as a pet.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.880
Absolutely not!

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:40.710
Why not? You don't like bugs?

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:48.260
It's the "keep" part that I'm worried about.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:52.770
I think it's been about ten years now.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:56.100
Back in my hometown, I kept a bird as a pet.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:01.400
A white bird named Kafu.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:02.860
Was it an evening kite?

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:04.990
I told you, he was a white bird.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:10.580
I say I kept him, but really I just fed him each morning.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:19.040
He just loved the minestrone I made!
His beak would be all red after eating it.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.930
But at some point he stopped showing up.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:29.010
I waited for him every day, but...

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.230
Oh, so you got dumped?

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:37.600
More, please!

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:41.900
Maybe it wasn't enough, just giving him one pot.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:48.200
He wasn't a glutton like you.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:50.490
That so?

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:02.460
Right here's just fine, thank you!

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.630
Thanks!

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:05.880
See you around.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.810
There sure are a lot of mountain tomatoes around here, huh?

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:15.930
Too bad their skin's too thick to eat.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.810
Maybe the bird will eat them.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:20.980
Are you sure Kafu really wasn't an evening kite?

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.860
Maybe he ate too many tomatoes and turned red.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:25.650
<i>That's</i> your theory?

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:29.780
We're at the mountaintop!

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:47.050
So, wanna eat a late-night snack until dawn breaks?

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:48.510
Late-night snack?

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:52.180
A peanut!

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:55.430
So that's what was in your bag...

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:57.640
Let's go halfsies!

00:06:58.730 --> 00:06:59.850
Thanks.

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:09.740
Hey, Hakumei...

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:14.830
It doesn't look like it's coming, does it?

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:18.290
Mmm. Well, whatever.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.960
We'll just have to come back here again together.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:22.580
Yeah.

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:25.960
Is there any minestrone left?

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:27.880
There's still enough for one more bowl.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.510
Here you go.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.230
The evening kite?

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:03.330
Whoa!

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.680
This is incredible.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.360
Look, Mikochi.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.780
It'll be dawn soon.

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:32.700
What are you going to wish for?

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:35.740
What? Um...

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:37.830
I didn't think of anything.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:39.660
Me neither!

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:44.870
Hey, Mikochi, do you know the origin of the name "evening kite"?

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:50.840
They say when it's bathed in the color of dusk, it's tinged crimson.

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:54.680
And so, when it's bathed in the pure white morning sun...

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:09.150
Kafu!

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:11.860
You really are Kafu, right?

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:13.940
B-Be careful, Mikochi!

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:20.910
Evening kite, this is my wish:

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:23.080
Drop us off at that house.

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:34.050
Thank you, Kafu.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:38.260
Hey, Hakumei! Help me out!

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:44.890
I'm going to make minestrone, and since Kafu will eat a lot,

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:47.310
I have to make ten pots worth!

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:50.230
So you really are a glutton after all.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:12.670
Gone with the wind, huh?

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:14.090
Yeah.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:16.550
Is that okay?

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:21.510
He'll be back one day when he wants more minestrone.

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:23.600
Maybe, but...

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:27.390
I meant we should have had him help us with the dresser.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:28.100
Oh!

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:49.370
Wow...

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:54.250
This wall sure is something to look at!

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:57.050
This isn't a wall—those are all shops, you know.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:11:00.340
It's the main draw of the harbor town Arabi:
Tsumiki Marketplace.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:03.850
Where are we headed right now?

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:08.810
To my favorite shop. Let's have them watch our things for a little while!

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:12.350
They'll really do that for you?
What kind of shop is it?

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:14.360
It's kind of a café-pub hybrid.

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:18.150
There are so few places to relax in a lively place like Arabi.

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:21.780
Though the owner can be a handful sometimes...

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:24.950
Well, here it is.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:29.160
Barkeep, are you here?

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:33.170
We haven't opened yet, Mikochi.

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.170
So you brought someone with you today?

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:38.800
I'm Hakumei. Nice to meetcha.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:39.840
Likewise.

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:43.300
Stocking up again?

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:47.010
Yes. The fish for sale in this town is a cut above.

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:49.270
Very glad you think so.

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:51.600
What do you think, Hakumei?

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:53.690
Do you like this little town of ours?

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:57.730
Sure do. These shops are selling so many things I've never seen before!

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:04.450
And Mikochi bought me a conch shell,
and after this we're going to look for my new mug.

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:06.160
So you've just been shopping?

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:10.290
Well, since you came all the way here,
I'll serve a bit of a delicacy.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:12.000
There you are.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.210
What is this?

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:14.630
It's pickled octopus!

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:18.630
You can grill it or eat it as-is. Goes with cold beer.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:23.090
You're right, I do want a drink now!

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:25.930
What would go with the dried sardines we bought today?

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:28.060
Gotta have cold sake for that!

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:30.850
Mikochi, let's buy some sake to take home!

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:35.480
We still have some at home, don't we?
Let's not waste our money.

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:39.690
We already spent quite a lot today,
so we have to save...

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:43.820
Care to try some pickled fish?

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:46.490
That doesn't seem like it'd go well with coffee.

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:47.990
Hm?

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:49.910
What's wrong, Mikochi?

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:57.330
Hakumei... Try to stay calm when I tell you this.

00:12:57.750 --> 00:12:58.920
Okay.

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:03.380
My wallet... is gone... I think.

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:05.090
Oh?

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:07.850
Please freak out a little bit!

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:14.890
Coming to stock up only to lose
your wallet. How stupid can you get?

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:15.890
What's this? What's this?
Coming to stock up only to lose
your wallet. How stupid can you get?

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:16.850
What's this? What's this?

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:24.700
Well then, how about going on a sightseeing tour to search for it?

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:25.740
What's this?

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:28.950
You'll need lunch if you're going on a day trip.

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:30.490
But I can't pay you...

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:35.210
Yes, well, this is Hakumei's first time here, isn't it? Show her around.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:38.960
Right. Thank you, ma'am.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:42.420
Oh! I know what this is! It's a siphon!

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:50.600
So, is that place the reason why you come home tipsy every now and again?

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:51.850
I suppose it is.

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:55.600
Hey, step right up!

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:58.730
Oh, Miko-chan, is that you?

00:13:58.730 --> 00:13:59.810
"Miko"?

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.020
If it isn't Fusenmaru-san!

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:03.530
Stocking up today?

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:06.030
No, we're... well...

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:08.110
She lost her wallet.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:09.530
Oh?

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:12.580
That's just awful. Wait there a second.

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:15.750
Did I do something wrong?

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.380
Um... What's this?

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:23.920
The latest batch of dried fish. Eat up and cheer up!

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:25.550
If you like it, then come on back again.

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:27.470
Th-Thank you.

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:31.430
What do you think you're doing, Fusenmaru?
Trying to make us look bad?

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:33.220
Mikochi-san, have some of this, too!

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:34.350
How about some tsukudani?

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:35.850
Have a taste of these pickles!

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:37.230
These were caught this morning!

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:38.440
I stewed this perch!

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:39.310
Marry me!

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:44.440
You sure are popular.

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:48.950
Let's leave these with the barkeep too
and maybe stick to the back streets from now on.

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:49.910
Yeah.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:15:00.620
Now, should we go through the back streets on Fishy Way or the western block's underground market...

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:02.840
What would you like to see, Hakumei?

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:04.800
I want to eat our lunch.

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:06.050
Then we'll go...

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:07.510
For lunch?

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:09.510
I've decided on our next destination.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:12.140
It's another one of my favorites.

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:22.060
There it is, there it is! Right inside here.

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:33.160
Wow...

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:37.910
This is the market square from when Tsumiki wasn't stacked so high.

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:41.040
It looks like it was whittled down by the light shining on it.

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:44.290
It's a good place to eat lunch, isn't it?

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:45.710
I was hoping you'd say that!

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:48.710
It's grilled pressed sushi!

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:50.420
There's ball-shaped sushi too!

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:53.050
Let's go halfsies! Halfsies!

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:57.060
Hakumei, you're eating the gari too fast.

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:02.020
Only a harbor town could have fish this tasty.

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:09.150
Since we've come all the way here, do you want to go to the port?

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:11.490
Yeah, let's go!

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:14.160
Then... if we go from here...

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:17.950
What's wrong?

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:23.290
Hakumei, if you see any blue cloth flags,
make sure you don't let <i>me</i> see them.

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:25.460
Uh... I'm on it!

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:30.760
Um, Mikochi?

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:33.880
The sweet smell of freshly woven fabric...

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.300
Is this Hiromuta cotton I feel?

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:38.810
Blended with thirty percent linen, perhaps?

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:41.890
I don't think there was any point in blindfolding you.

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:46.940
I'm sorry. I just can't help myself around cloth.

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:50.610
Then it must be torture not having any money, huh?

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:53.150
Well, wait a second.

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:56.870
So I do have some! I just forgot to use it.

00:16:57.160 --> 00:17:00.700
Can you buy that Hiromuta cotton stuff with this?

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:06.080
It's a lovely thought, but one bundle is tens of thousands of yen.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:07.710
That much?

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:12.170
Its finely spun thread comes from cotton picked in West Hiromuta

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:15.220
and is woven into top quality cloth by the craftsmen there.

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:22.310
In the past, when I was a part-time dressmaker,
I received a bolt from my boss.

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:24.690
What happened to that cloth, then?

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:32.030
My needlework skills were lacking—
all the seams ended up puckered.

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:37.700
The fabric I longed for became the fabric of my worst nightmare.

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:42.540
Well, first of all, you have to get used to the fabric.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.710
Here it is, here it is!

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:49.130
*Oba-chan, is this Hiromuta?
And do you have it in red?

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:52.840
How much is this? Seven hundred yen? I won't go higher than five hundred!

00:17:57.340 --> 00:17:59.050
And there you go.

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:01.850
A scarf! Are you sure?

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:06.020
It's a souvenir. Think of it as a thank-you gift for showing me around.

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:09.230
Thank you, Hakumei.

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:15.280
This fabric is... fifty percent Hiromuta-style cotton, fifty percent linen, right?

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:17.490
What an awful special talent.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:19.700
It's very cheap!

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:25.910
From here on is the inside market.
When we come out, we'll be at the harbor.

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:28.420
This is the most hubbub we've seen all day.

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:32.420
Even this is still on the calm side.
The auction is over and everything.

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:34.210
Hey, Mikochi-chan!

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:34.880
Huh?

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:36.970
Sekimenmaru-san.

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:39.090
You came at just the right time!

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:42.350
What do you think of this
soy sauce? It's for a marinade.

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:48.980
It's delicious, but I think it might be better if the Japanese pepper were more coarsely ground.

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:51.360
Ah, I see.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:53.440
Try the stock for my sake lees soup too!

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:54.780
This namerou, too.

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:56.610
Which sake should season the salmon?

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:59.320
Um... Right now I'm kind of...

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:03.370
Go ahead. I'll look around on my own a little bit.

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:04.660
But...

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:06.160
It's okay, go ahead!

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:08.790
Sorry, I'll be done soon!

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:12.250
Wow...

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:17.260
Put a bit more minced ginger on top.
Oh, maybe myoga ginger would also work.

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:22.260
You decreased the amount of shiso, I see.
How about adding some sesame miso?

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:26.770
If you want citrus flavor, yuzu would definitely make a better seasoning than sudachi.

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:28.350
What in the world is this fish?

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:30.020
That's the red bigeye.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:31.310
Whoa!

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:37.860
No one's here, huh?

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:41.030
The fishermen will all be at home drinking by now.

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:45.160
Everything just fell silent.
It feels out of place, doesn't it?

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:46.240
Oh, yeah?

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:52.120
When it's busy, it kind of feels like the town's shouting, "Get moving!"

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:55.630
That's a town where time passes quickly.

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:56.960
You think so?

00:19:56.960 --> 00:20:00.630
When I see this hustle and bustle,
I feel like time stops.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:02.720
The sun sunk its harpoon into the tide
(Ho!)
When I see this hustle and bustle,
I feel like time stops.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:05.850
I see... I don't really get it.
The sun sunk its harpoon into the tide
(Ho!)

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:14.520
The sun sunk its harpoon into the tide
(Ho!)

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:15.860
When it saw the wall of light across the waves
(A-hey!)

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:16.770
A song?
When it saw the wall of light across the waves
(A-hey!)

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:17.230
When it saw the wall of light across the waves
(A-hey!)

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:20.820
A sea shanty. It's closing time at the market.
When it saw the wall of light across the waves
(A-hey!)

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:27.280
When it saw the wall of light across the waves
(A-hey!)

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:37.170
The frogs on their way home set the gillnet
(Heave-ho!)

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:43.630
For the school of little sardines

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:50.220
Not yet, not yet—the sun still shines
(Heave-ho!)

00:20:50.220 --> 00:21:10.370
Send it off! Heave-ho we sent 'em off! The harpoon and the song

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:17.750
So, shall we head home?

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:19.790
But what about the wallet?

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:22.010
I think we've looked enough.

00:21:28.140 --> 00:21:30.470
My wallet?

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:32.970
I've kept my eye on it since I picked it up.

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:35.640
I couldn't seem to get hold of you, Mikochi-san.

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:39.360
Well... I apologize for causing you trouble.

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:42.980
If you want to shop, there are a few places still open.

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:46.360
My legs are already so stiff...

00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:47.950
Oh, that's right!

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:51.990
There was one thing I really wanted to buy.

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:54.410
Huh? What?

00:21:57.420 --> 00:22:00.040
Barkeep, we're back!

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:03.760
It smells good in here!

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:07.090
Hey, I've been waiting for you.

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:12.760
We'll be having quite the drinking party tonight!

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:13.560
Yummy!

00:22:13.560 --> 00:22:16.770
We're going to be here all night, aren't we?

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:22.570
So, did you buy anything interesting?

00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:23.360
Hm?

00:22:23.780 --> 00:22:25.400
One minute.

00:22:28.150 --> 00:22:30.990
This! Pour my next one in this!

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:34.240
Well, isn't that a nice mug.

00:22:34.240 --> 00:22:37.540
It is! It's the same design as Mikochi's but a different color!

00:22:37.540 --> 00:22:40.830
I'm sure we're going to get them mixed up.

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:42.170
That's okay, right?

00:22:47.220 --> 00:22:55.310
When the breeze is pleasant, let's eat outside

00:22:55.310 --> 00:23:03.110
The olives are fragrant this time of year

00:23:03.110 --> 00:23:07.110
And in the plum-colored sky,

00:23:07.110 --> 00:23:11.070
the stars twinkle and shine

00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:15.620
After we take in an easy breath,

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:20.000
the banquet will begin!

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:23.590
A freshly-made smoked cheese quiche,

00:23:23.590 --> 00:23:27.340
sockeye salmon wrapped in magnolia leaves

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:31.260
Look, the whole world is rejoicing

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:36.100
It's itching to dance with us

00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:40.060
And what drink might fit a night like this?

00:23:40.060 --> 00:23:44.020
How about something botanical with pepper in it?

00:23:44.020 --> 00:23:49.320
We could even catch the moon with our tiny hands

00:23:49.320 --> 00:23:52.860
At least, that's how we're feeling
